Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:59:50 +0900
Subject: Phone frames are held while the phone surface is gone,
 so KWin stops drawing with the screen off

With the screen off (or the app in the background) the host presents nothing for the phone, but
each new frame KWin committed got the previous one reported discarded at once, and KWin counts a
discarded frame as done: it composited every client update (a blinking cursor, a window writing
its state) for nothing. mibook measured KWin at 6.7% of a core over 4 h 25 min of standby with two
test windows open. Superseded phone frames are now held as for a paced output: KWin stops at two
pending frames until the surface is back, when render_all reports them discarded. Cast sources and
agent workspaces are decided as before.

